   "gap": "Reconstruct the selected estimation arguments of Fisher 1922 with exact regularity conditions, giving each estimate and theorem explicit model, sampling and regularity scope, for the parts of the complete original estimation/information/sufficiency presentation that are still absent: (a) s.10, efficiency of the method of moments for the Pearsonian curves (pp. 342-355), and s.11, the reason for that efficiency in a small region near the normal curve (pp. 355-356); (b) s.12, the Poisson series (p. 359 ff.) and estimation in a dilution series (pp. 363-366); (c) the multiparameter (joint) maximum-likelihood asymptotic theorem, with the inverse information matrix as asymptotic covariance, on which Fisher's Type III joint statements and his p.337 inference to 100 per cent efficiency of m+a(p+1) rest; body lines 338-341 and 403-412 state that this analogue is not proved; (d) existence and limit law of the grouped (class-likelihood) maximum likelihood estimate, the fixed-grid periodic remainder for grouped information, and goodness-of-fit calibration of Fisher's L / Pearson's chi-square, which fisher-grouping-and-moments.tex lines 207-219 and 350-362 record as not established.",
